{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P17796","uniProtkbId":"VIRB6_AGRFC","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"1990-08-01","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-11-04","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"1990-11-01","entryVersion":118,"sequenceVersion":2},"annotationScore":4.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Agrobacterium fabrum (strain C58 / ATCC 33970)","commonName":"Agrobacterium tumefaciens (strain C58)","taxonId":176299,"lineage":["Bacteria","Pseudomonadati","Pseudomonadota","Alphaproteobacteria","Hyphomicrobiales","Rhizobiaceae","Rhizobium/Agrobacterium group","Agrobacterium","Agrobacterium tumefaciens complex"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Type IV secretion system protein VirB6"}}},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2194232"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2233252"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2370849"}],"value":"virB6"},"orderedLocusNames":[{"value":"Atu6172"}],"orfNames":[{"value":"AGR_pTi_10"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"O50333"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P09779"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10913084"}],"value":"Component of the VirB/VirD4 type IV secretion system (T4SS), which translocates transfer DNA (T-DNA) and virulence effector proteins into plant host cells, leading to crown gall disease (PubMed:10913084). The VirB6 subunit plays a role in T-pilus biogenesis (PubMed:10913084). It may serve as a platform for the recruitment of the VirB2 pilin subunit and for pilus assembly (By similarity). It is also involved in T4SS assembly and function (By similarity). It has a stabilizing effect on VirB5 accumulation, thereby regulating T-pilus assembly (PubMed:10913084). It is required for the formation of VirB7 homodimers, which may function in T-pilus biogenesis (PubMed:10913084)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"O50333"}],"value":"The core secretion machinery of the VirB/VirD4 T4SS is composed of cytoplasmic ATPases that form the energy center, an inner membrane complex (IMC), an outer membrane core complex (OMCC) and a stalk (or cylinder) that connects the IMC and the OMCC (By similarity). This subunit is embedded into the inner membrane and is part of the stalk (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29976757"}],"value":"Localizes to a cell pole"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10913084"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29976757"}],"value":"Cell inner membrane","id":"SL-0037"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}],"value":"Multi-pass membrane protein","id":"SL-9909"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10913084"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29976757"}],"value":"The deletion mutant is avirulent on K.daigremontiana (PubMed:10913084). T-pili are not formed (PubMed:10913084, PubMed:29976757). Deletion of the gene leads to reduced cellular levels of VirB3, VirB5 and VirB7 (PubMed:10913084). The formation of VirB7 homodimers is abolished, but the levels of VirB7 monomers and VirB7-VirB9 heterodimers are not affected (PubMed:10913084)"}],"commentType":"DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the TrbL/VirB6 family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":295,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Type IV secretion system protein VirB6","featureId"